if heading in text:text=text.split(heading)[0].rstrip()+'\n'
text+='\n'+heading+'\n\nThe actual identity workspace reader is paired with SCI\'s `8531226d` writer on qualified input `'+head+'`. Five actual PostgreSQL domain roots and seven existing installation-wide HTTPS roots passed in `'+consumer.name+'`. The domain tests cover the restricted principal, non-default and disabled workspace history, exact database tenant/site/cell attribution, bounded safe payload, foreign/missing scope and forged context, assistant pagination, four concurrent reads, append refusal and explicit repair, and cancellation while the real INSERT is blocked after its page read. Existing current-session/audience refusals remain covered. Initial direct-insert timestamp and unsupported category/audience fixture failures are retained. The corrected projection fixes the existing `to` bound to the database clock before access appends and leaves the public filter allowlist unchanged.\n\nTwo actual scoped COMMIT wire-loss subcases exposed no page, cursor or assistant map. Withheld COMMIT left zero events; a suppressed server acknowledgement left one. Each attempt issued one COMMIT, and an explicit retry appended one new event. The installation-wide HTTPS regressions, including their four wire-loss subcases, passed on the same source. No private chain-head read privilege was added.\n\nRepository checks, builds and all test stages passed in current stage `'+stage.name+'`; '+browser+' Fixtures used pinned PostgreSQL 18.6/pgvector 0.8.7 on owned network-none Linux arm64 containers with protected SCRAM input files and no host ports. They were removed. This qualifies the existing Go consumer and preserves the published installation-wide route; it creates no workspace HTTP route or new rendered UI/amd64 claim. The complete AUD-108 item remains open for DEV public-contract metadata, installed-flow qualification and Delivery collector admission/reconciliation.\n'
